 happens i was there  he knew it wasn't there it's that guy  he's mostly in his feelings about the  loss of his best friend natasha as we  see his mind wander after the musical  version natasha starts cartwheeling  around it's here that he takes a break  and leaves to go to the restroom and we  also see him fumble with his hearing aid  it turns out clint has suffered some  severe hearing loss in his left ear  thanks to his adventures with the  avengers it looks like clint is making  up for lost time with his kids and is  spending the days leading up to  christmas with them laura is off at  their farmhouse and explains their  separation by suggesting this is  supposed to be clint's one-on-one time  with his kids of course clintus pulled  away from his family after spotting kate  on tv in the ronin suit from avengers  end game  we're introduced to two villains in the  first episode of hawkeye one is the  tracksuit mafia who are truly living up  to their marvel comics hype we don't  really get a sense of who they are and  why they're so angry but we do know that  they had run-ins with ronin when he was  still on his killing rampage after the  snap they chased down kate after she  fumbles their heist of the secret black  market auction but clint comes to save  the day after he sees his ronin suit  back on the streets of new york kate  snatched it during the auction chaos  while jack made off with ronin's sword  speaking of jack this is another villain  we need to keep our eye on he has  suspiciously wooed kate's widow mother  and the pair are now engaged he loves  swords which is no surprise given jack  is pulled directly from the marvel  comics character jacques du kane aka  swordsman a former mentor and teacher of  clans jacques has no connection with  kate bishop in the comic so this is an  interesting twist hawkeye is giving us  while we don't know what jack is up to  in episode 1 his creepiness alone lets  us know he's up to no good it's already  suspected that he's involved in the  death of his uncle armand and there's  some talk at the auction of a sizable  inheritance while episode 1 served as an  introduction to kate her mother eleanor  jack the tracksuit mafia oh and we can't  forget lucky the pizza dog it gave us a  good idea of where hawkeye is going and  themes that will be carried throughout  clint is clearly still dealing with the  grief of losing natasha while he also  seems to be trying to cover up his past  as ronin he still has enemies from his  days as the vigilante and they're coming  back to haunt him thanks to his number  one fan kate kate a vigilante in her own  right is now working to uncover the  mystery of her future step dad and the  murder of armond iii who in the comics  is actually jack's father she's become  the target of the tracksuit mafia who  are clearly not the men in charge we  suspect kate and clint will find out  they somehow have a connection to one  another especially given how all these  characters intertwine in the comics and  then there's the lingering mystery of  that watch which is very important to  the tracksuit mafia for some unknown  reason we've got 90 seconds to find a  watch everything else is second there  episode 2 picks up immediately after  episode 1 as clint barton is pulling the  ronin mask off of kate bishop in an  alley clint is keen on getting his suit  back from kate so they head to her  apartment to hide out for a moment while  still in shock that she's with the real  hawkeye kate changes and hands the suit  over to clint unfortunately those pesky  tracksuit mafia members have tracked  them down and start throwing molotov  cocktails through her apartment window  the apartment eventually catches fire  causing the duo to abandon the ronin  suits and now kate and clint are on the  run  once the tracksuit mafia sets kate's  apartment on fire the duo has to bolt  and head somewhere safe kate decides to  go to her aunt's apartment since she's  out of town clint forces kate to hide  out there while he heads back to  retrieve the suit he finds out one of  the firemen stole it which is just  another unnecessary obstacle for clint  to overcome he comes back to visit kate  and helps her patch up a wound and we  get a peek at how clint might become a  father figure to his new friend the  following day clint has to ditch his  kids as he sends him off to be with  their very understanding mom he revisits  kate back at their hideout and then they  go their separate ways but not before  exchanging phone numbers clint thinks  this is the last time he'll see kate and  begs her only to call if she has an  emergency it's now clint's mission to  retrieve the ronin suit and figure out  why the tracksuit mafia is stirring up  trouble yet again he travels to a  live-action roleplay event to find his  suit where he suspects the thieving  firefighter will be wearing it clint  must sign up and participate in the  event to get to the firefighter which  turns into one of the best slow motion  bits ever seen in the mcu as clint fake  slices and dices some hilarious  adversaries after a duel with the thief  clint is finally in possession of the  ronin suit again  back at kate's mom's penthouse jack is  back doing very jack things he continues  to fool kate's mom while not bullying  his soon-to-be daughter-in-law but he  also doesn't seem to care kate ends up  challenging him to a fencing match where  he pretends to be the lesser competitor  as kate yells at jack to stop letting  her win she eventually tricks him into  showing off his true talent and uses  this as a way to prove he's some kind of  liar sorry for scaring you into telling  the truth  obviously jack is a liar but we're still  not sure what his true intentions are  he's still in possession of the ronin  sword but it's unclear what his plan is  after his fencing match with kate he  offers her a butterscotch one which  matches those in a bowl at armand's  house from episode 1. this appears to be  enough proof for kate that jack killed  ramon but in reality all it suggests is  that jack has been to his uncle's house  before jack's involvement with his  uncle's death is still unclear but  things don't look good  while kate is having some family fun  clint sets himself up to be kidnapped by  the tracksuit mafia he tells his wife on  the phone that he's doing a catch and  release which laura points out is  classic gnat after luring the goons to  him glint is taken to a secret location  where he continues to tell the gangsters  he wants to talk to the person in charge  after realizing clint's in trouble kate  comes to help after tracking his  location but falls through the roof of  the building and causes a mess instead  as kate and clint are tied up by the  gang one of the mafia members goes into  a speaker-filled room to get the boss as  the base in the background booms we get  our first look at maya lopez aka echo  it's a briefest of glimpses as the  screen cuts the credits after we see her  face but it promises us an even bigger  episode for next week echo who already  has her own series coming to disney plus  is a deaf hero who is mainly known for  her role in the daredevil comics the  adoptive daughter of kingpin echo's  appearance in hawkeye might hint that we  could be getting a second go-round with  wilson fisk from the netflix daredevil  series or the mcu could remix her origin  the way it's done with plenty of other  heroes while it looks like ekko is the  villain now we can almost guarantee she  won't be there is either a bigger threat  we haven't met or jack truly is the big  bad the biggest takeaway from hawkeye  episode 2 still no yelena biloba from  black widow as promised but we expect  she's right around the corner  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  hawkeye are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

